.TH HYDD 8 "2026-11-22" "hydd 0.4.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
hydd \- read-only Hydrus Public Tag Repository mirror daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hydd
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hydd
keeps a local, read-only mirror of the Hydrus Public Tag Repository (PTR)
and answers Hydrus Client API queries about file hashes in the same JSON
language as the Python Hydrus client.
.PP
The PTR is a centralized Hydrus server, not a peer-to-peer network. It stores
SHA-256 file hashes and their tag mappings, plus a small number of legacy
SHA-1/MD5 hashes from very old files; it does not store the files
themselves. The default repository is
.BR https://ptr.hydrus.network:45871 .
.PP
On first start
.B hydd
downloads the repository update stream, builds a compact immutable store, and
then periodically applies new updates. It never uploads tags, petitions, or
account data.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Configuration file. Default:
.IR /etc/hydd.conf .
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-data\-dir " " \fIPATH\fR
Override the configured data directory.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-listen " " \fIADDRESS\fR
Override the API listen address.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Override the API listen port.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sync
Serve the existing store without contacting the repository or applying
updates.
.TP
.B \-\-sync\-once
Run one sync pass, building the store if necessary, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-query " " HASH
Print the storage and display tags for a file hash (64-character SHA-256,
40-character SHA-1, or 32-character MD5), then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-compact
Merge the append-only delta journal into the immutable base store, then exit.
With
.B compression = false
it runs SQLite VACUUM. This never discards live tags or mappings.
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-store
Open and validate the store, print its counts, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-scan\-updates
Parse every cached update file with the current importer, report any file
that would make the sync fail, and exit. Useful before a long initial build.
.TP
.B \-\-stats
Query the running local API and print repository statistics, sync state,
live initial-build progress, and an estimate of when the next PTR update
will be applied. Does not need root or access to the data directory.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-access\-key
Print the API access key and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " " LEVEL
One of
.IR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error ", " off .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help summary.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hydd.conf
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I /var/lib/hyd
Default data directory. Contains the store, delta journal, sync state, and
generated keys.
.TP
.I /var/lib/hyd/api_access_key
Generated API access key (mode 0600).
.TP
.I /var/lib/hyd/service_key
Generated service key reported by the Client API.
.TP
.I /var/log/hyd/hyd.log
Rotating plaintext log. Old logs are gzipped as
.IR hyd.log.1.gz " ... " hyd.log.5.gz .
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration is a simple
.I key = value
file. The most important settings are:
.TP
.B data_dir
Data directory. Default
.IR /var/lib/hyd .
.TP
.B listen_address ", " listen_port
API listener. Defaults to
.I 127.0.0.1:45869
(loopback only).
.TP
.B access_key ", " access_key_file
API access key, either inline or read/generated from a file.
.TP
.B repository_url ", " repository_access_key
PTR address and the shared read-only key. The defaults point at the real PTR.
.TP
.B sync_enabled ", " sync_on_start ", " sync_interval_seconds
Background sync policy.
.TP
.B compression
Select the storage backend.
.I true
(the default) uses the compact custom columnar store.
.I false
uses a plain SQLite database at
.IR <data_dir>/sqlite/hyd.sqlite3 .
Switching backends requires a fresh data directory.
.TP
.B partitions
Custom-store partition count; must be a power of two. More partitions use less
RAM during the initial build but make more passes over the update files.
.TP
.B compaction_enabled ", " compact_after_delta_mb
Whether and when to merge the delta journal into the base store. Compaction
is enabled by default and never drops live data.
.TP
.B keep_update_cache
Keep downloaded update files after the initial build. Default false.
.TP
.B log_file ", " log_rotate_mb ", " log_rotate_keep ", " log_rotate_compress
Rotating gzip log. Defaults:
.IR /var/log/hyd/hyd.log ", 10 MiB, 5 files, enabled."
.TP
.B max_download_bytes ", " max_update_index
Development/test limits. Automated tests must stay under 10 GiB of downloads.
.SH API
The following read-only Client API endpoints are implemented:
.PP
.nf
GET  /api_version
GET  /session_key
GET  /verify_access_key
GET  /client_info
GET  /get_services
GET  /get_service
GET  /get_files/file_metadata
GET  /get_files/file_hashes
GET  /health              (hydd extension)
GET  /stats               (hydd extension: /health superset)
.fi
.PP
Every endpoint except
.IR / ", " /api_version ", " /health ", " /stats
requires the
.B Hydrus-Client-API-Access-Key
header, the
.B Hydrus-Client-API-Session-Key
header, or the same parameter in the query string or JSON body. Missing keys
return 401, invalid keys 403, and expired session keys 419.
.PP
The server speaks JSON only. CBOR requests return 406. File and thumbnail
endpoints return 404 because the mirror stores no files. Search and mutation
endpoints return 501.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run one sync and exit:
.PP
.nf
    hydd --sync-once
.fi
.PP
Show repository statistics from the running daemon (no root needed):
.PP
.nf
    hydd --stats
.fi
.PP
Look up a file:
.PP
.nf
    hydd --query 4c77267f93415de0bc33b7725b8c331a809a924084bee03ab2f5fae1c6019eb2
.fi
.PP
Query the running API:
.PP
.nf
    curl -H "Hydrus-Client-API-Access-Key: $(hydd --print-access-key)" \\
         'http://127.0.0.1:45869/get_files/file_metadata?hashes=%5B%22...%22%5D'
.fi
.SH SECURITY
The API requires a key and listens on loopback by default. It uses plain HTTP;
for remote access, place it behind a TLS reverse proxy. Keep
.I /etc/hydd.conf
and the generated key files readable only by the
.I hyd
user.
.SH NOTES
A full PTR mirror is large: the October 2026 QuickSync archive was 50.6 GB
compressed and 160 GB extracted. hydd's compact read-only store is much
smaller (roughly 25-30 GB), but a full initial sync needs room for the
downloaded update stream and temporary definition files (several GB) in
addition to the final store; plan for about 40-45 GB free.
With
.B compression = false
the SQLite mirror is roughly 45-60 GB. Changing compression after a store
exists is refused; use a fresh data directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR hydd.conf (5),
.IR https://hydrusnetwork.github.io/hydrus/ .
